==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|δέον||that which is binding, needful, right, proper|tr=deon|lang=grc}} + {{term|-logy||argument|lang=en}}, c. 1826.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{context|ethics|lang=en}} The [[ethical]] study of [[duties]], [[obligation]]s, and [[right]]s, with an approach focusing on the [[rightness]] or [[wrongness]] of actions themselves and not on the [[goodness]] or [[badness]] of the [[consequence]]s of those actions.

====Coordinate terms====
* [[consequentialism]]
* [[utilitarianism]]

